  "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds an exact construction and minimum-query classification for the 62 five-source affine parity-hyperplane output families under the existing dirty binary connector contract. Ten source-coordinate symmetry classes suffice. The minima are 38, 40, 42, and 44 complete calls. The odd-weight family is the exceptional 44-call case: exhaustive enumeration shows no restored ten-toggle word covers all 16 odd masks, and a twelve-toggle construction attains the exact lower bound.\n\nThe package includes explicit source walks and boundary-pair readouts for all 62 families, a proof of the prefix-difference identity and lower bounds, a 945-word certificate, and a separate perfect-matching enumerator with negative controls. It keeps the connector alphabet fixed and does not instantiate a selected supplier or claim a new kappa.\n\n## Pins and reproduction\n\n- Base: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`\n- Seed: `595e2bb0d08b79ae735ee7050a352198`; track `recursive-interfaces`; task card `connector-alphabet-change` with documented scope change.\n- Selected record SHA256: `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`\n- `python3 -I -B research/five-source-parity-hyperplanes-seed595e/verify.py`\n- `python3 -I -B research/five-source-parity-hyperplanes-seed595e/independent_check.py`\n- `python3 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/five-source-parity-hyperplanes-seed595e --check-only`\n- `make selected-record-check`\n\nThe first two commands pass under Python 3.14.7. The registered Python 3.12 replay could not be run because Python 3.12 is unavailable in this environment. The repository metadata/pins check and selected-record check pass.\n\n## Scope and attribution\n\nThe result is exact only for five source labels, the fixed binary connector alphabet, unit cost per complete call including fixed-width dispatch, and affine-hyperplane output families. All source, connector, and output states may be dirty. No helper, copy, frame transition, or supplier-specific child profile is included. The selected frontier and kappa remain unchanged.\n\nPredecessor attribution and source pins are in the package's `NOTICE.md` and `SOURCES.json`. Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance in scope selection, derivation, implementation, checking, and writing; no independent human review is claimed.\n",
